# Buildspace-owned navigation

Perso's Buildspaces children now derive from the saved buildspace IDs and names supplied by the buildspace owner. The fixed Broccoli child and its standalone connection special case were removed. No playground-specific channel was added.

The shared channel navigation component accepts validated catalog updates while retaining mounted content, selection and expansion state. Saving a buildspace notifies subscribers, so additions and renames update the sidebar without replacing the current draft. Pins obtain the updated catalog through the same navigation contract.

Channel activation carries the actual buildspace identity. Directory Open, direct child selection and reload agree on the selected space. Initial activation is awaited; stale activation cannot override a later selection. Node and review links in the same buildspace are preserved, while cross-space navigation clears unrelated node/chat selections.

The live application was restarted. An isolated browser inspection confirmed both Personal buildspace and Ergonomics playground in the sidebar; selecting the latter opened its populated board with the matching channel/space ID and no browser errors. Screenshots were inspected. No real user draft, provider call, approval, commit or merge was performed.

This working-tree correction follows immutable review target 231. Its separate evidence does not alter or claim coverage from that older candidate's checks.

Verification: build and final syntax check passed; all 130 server tests passed. The browser checkpoint passed 97 tests and exposed eight node/deep-link failures during the intermediate implementation. After correcting same-space deep-link preservation, all 11 tests in the affected files passed unchanged. Dynamic channel creation/rename, correct board identity, reload, draft preservation, dirty-editor guards and late-response protection passed focused checks. Both Perso acceptance tests passed with the reviewed recording updated to remove the obsolete fixed channel and pin.
